            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0214" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4 A 2/92: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cottrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-09-17T09:00:00-04:32"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                                1924—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:35
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>28. Department’s telegram no. 19, September 11, 10 p.m.<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d49-f1"/> Foreign Office informs me delegate has been appointed to
                    opium conference but impossible to restrict cultivation of coca leaf plant. Full
                    report by mail.<anchor n="85" xml:id="d49-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cottrell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
